{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "laplace_beltrami_lon_periodic_lat_zero_grad",
    "description": "METRIC spherical Laplacian (Laplace-Beltrami) of a scalar field on a REGIONAL latlon patch: matches the bare open-namespace rewrite-target {op: laplacian, args: [u]} (esm-spec 9.6.8/4.2 author sugar with no evaluable core) constrained by where {u:{shape:[lon,lat]}}, exactly mirroring grids/mpas/rules/fv_laplacian_cell -- a rule MAY match laplacian directly and emit a one-shot scheme rather than route through the nested-D identity. Emits the metric-weighted makearray for lap u = (1/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi)) d2u/dlambda^2 + (1/(R_sphere^2 cos phi)) d/dphi(cos phi du/dphi) (lambda=lon, phi=lat, RADIANS: dlambda=(pi/180)dlon_deg, dphi=(pi/180)dlat_deg, pi=3.141592653589793). The doubly-interior region [2,NLON-1]x[2,NLAT-1] imports stencils/laplace_beltrami_interior; the eight boundary regions tile the frame with two independent, composable closures. LONGITUDE = PERIODIC (the patch spans the full zonal circle, NLON dlon_deg=360): the i=1 and i=NLON columns wrap the zonal second difference (i-1->NLON at i=1, i+1->1 at i=NLON), following the central_D2_lon_periodic precedent. LATITUDE = ZERO-GRADIENT (homogeneous Neumann band edges): the mimetic meridional flux through the outer face is dropped, giving one-sided rows j=1: cos(phi_{3/2})(u[i,2]-u[i,1])/(R_sphere^2 cos phi_1 dphi^2) and j=NLAT: cos(phi_{NLAT-1/2})(u[i,NLAT-1]-u[i,NLAT])/(R_sphere^2 cos phi_NLAT dphi^2), the cos-weighted analogue of central_D2_lat_zero_grad_bc's ghost-elimination. cos(phi) at cell centers and faces is computed in the RUNTIME rule body from phi_j=(pi/180)(lat0_deg+(j-1)dlat_deg) and phi_{j+-1/2}=(pi/180)(lat0_deg+(j-1+-1/2)dlat_deg); the free names R_sphere, dlon_deg, dlat_deg, lat0_deg resolve in the consuming model's scope (grids/latlon/grid.esm keyed-factor contract). POLE SINGULARITY (the crux, deliberately avoided here): the zonal weight 1/cos^2 phi diverges at phi=+-90, so this rule is DEFINED ONLY on a regional patch with lat in (lat0,lat1) strictly inside (-90,90) (a Laplace-Beltrami on a spherical band/cap where cos phi is bounded away from 0). The GLOBAL pole-cap Laplacian -- an averaged polar-cap closure or an unstructured cap that removes the 1/cos^2 singularity -- is a documented FOLLOW-UP, not this rule. ACCURACY: 2nd order in both L2 and Linf on a regional band with a pole-supercompatible (boundary-vanishing) field; annihilates constants (every second difference is zero) and the meridional flux form is discretely conservative through the band interior. Match scoping mirrors fv_laplacian_cell: the where shape constraint fires only on the laplacian of a bare field over THIS grid's lon x lat index sets and, under esm-spec 9.7.7 import renaming, the shape follows the renamed axes so two latlon patches coexist; a consumer taking laplacian of a compound inline expression must first bind it to a declared lon x lat observed.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:latlon",
      "op:laplacian",
      "order:2",
      "bc:periodic",
      "bc:zero_gradient",
      "axes:lon,lat",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Williamson, D. L., Drake, J. B., Hack, J. J., Jakob, R., & Swarztrauber, P. N. (1992). A standard test set for numerical approximations to the shallow water equations in spherical geometry. Journal of Computational Physics, 102(1), 211-224."
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (Neumann boundary by dropping the boundary flux) and Chapter 2 (the flux-form finite-volume Laplacian)."
      }
    ]
  },
